## Stopping the agent

```bash
# Disable scheduled runs (modern launchctl — load/unload are deprecated)
launchctl bootout "gui/$(id -u)/com.{{ user_short }}.night-shift-routine"

# Re-enable
launchctl bootstrap "gui/$(id -u)" ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.{{ user_short }}.night-shift-routine.plist
```

## Uninstalling

Easiest: `night-shift uninstall` (the CLI helper unloads every plist this install created + removes them — keeps your install dir + data).

Manual:

```bash
# Stop scheduled runs
launchctl bootout "gui/$(id -u)/com.{{ user_short }}.night-shift-routine" 2>/dev/null
rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.{{ user_short }}.night-shift-routine.plist

# Remove install
rm -rf {{ install_dir }}
rm -rf ~/.config/night-shift-agent
rm -rf ~/.cache/night-shift-agent

# Remove CLI symlink (if you added one)
rm -f ~/.local/bin/night-shift
```

## Troubleshooting

**Agent didn't run last night?**
```bash
night-shift logs 100      # See what happened
night-shift status        # Check if launchd is loaded
```

**Patches don't apply cleanly?**
The patch was generated against an older version of your code. Try:
```bash
night-shift apply <id> --force  # 3-way merge
```

**Want to roll back what the agent did to your project?**
```bash
night-shift restore       # Restore to last-night snapshot (passive baseline)
```

**Wifi flaked overnight?**
Check the log for `network_probe_failed`. The agent should have auto-recovered.

**Mac slept mid-run?**
Check that the launchd plist + caffeinate are both working. The agent should have prevented sleep.

